title: Paths in the Scene view
intro: Drag a moving platform's points and an enemy's patrol route right in the Scene view.
project: Platformer | Scene Paths

chapter: Mover points | Select a mover, drag its points
select: Lift
look: -11, -1, 6
say: This lift goes straight up and down. Its path used to be a line of numbers in the Inspector.
explain: handle:Mover.1 | Point 1 | Now each point on a selected mover's path has a knob. Drag it, and the path follows.
path: Ctrl+Mover.1 = 3, 6
expectvalue: Lift.Mover.Points = 3 6
explain: handle:Mover.+2 | Add a point | The small plus past the end adds a point. Drag it out to where the lift should go next.
path: Ctrl+Mover.+2 = 6, 6
explain: handle:Mover.+1 | Add between | Pluses between two points add one in the middle, for a corner.
path: Ctrl+Mover.+1 = 0, 3
expectvalue: Lift.Mover.Points = 0 3; 3 6; 6 6
explain: field:Mover.Points | Points | The Inspector keeps up, so the numbers are still there when you want them. Holding control snaps to half units.
say: Double-click a point to take it off. Each drag is one step to undo.
removepoint: Mover.3
expectvalue: Lift.Mover.Points = 0 3; 3 6
key: Ctrl+Z
expectvalue: Lift.Mover.Points = 0 3; 3 6; 6 6

chapter: Patrol routes | Left and Right turns
select: Slime
look: -8, 2.5, 4
say: A patrolling slime used to walk until it hit a wall or an edge. Now it can keep to a stretch of a long floor.
explain: handle:Patrol.Right | Right | Its route shows both ways out from where it's placed. A hollow knob means it walks on until a wall.
path: Ctrl+Patrol.Right = 2
expectvalue: Slime.Patrol.Right = 2
path: Ctrl+Patrol.Left = 2.5
expectvalue: Slime.Patrol.Left = 2.5
explain: field:Patrol.Left | Left and Right | Drag a turn and its Left or Right follows. Drag it back past the slime to clear it.
play
say: Now it turns at each end of its route, and if the player knocks it back, it walks back to its route.
wait: 4
stop
